ide platform.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** Only a one-time startup self-check exists; scheduled drift detection and alert response would live outside this repo\n29\t\n30\t(no evidence cited)\n31\t\n32\t## C04.2\n33\t\n34\t**Check:** The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events.\n35\t\n36\t**How to verify:** 1) Find what triggers the drift check: cron or CI schedule, admission webhook, or change events. 2) Check it runs for each agent deployment, not once for the fleet or only by hand. 3) Answer no if it is manual-only or covers only some deployments. Answer unknown if scheduling is set outside this repo.\n37\t\n38\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n39\t\n40\t**Reviewer's note:** Only a one-time startup self-check exists; scheduled drift detection and alert response would live outside this repo\n41\t\n42\t(no evidence cited)\n43\t\n44\t## C04.3\n45\t\n46\t**Check:** Detected drift triggers an alert and a set response (block, quarantine, or rollback) defined in config, with a time limit.\n47\t\n48\t**How to verify:** 1) Open the drift check's result handling. 2) Check drift raises an alert and triggers a response set in config: block, quarantine, or rollback. 3) Check a time limit is set. 4) Answer no if drift only logs, the response or time limit is missing, or a check error is treated as no drift.\n49\t\n50\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n51\t\n52\t**Reviewer's note:** Only a one-time startup self-check exists; scheduled drift detection and alert response would live outside this repo\n53\t\n54\t(no evidence cited)\n55\t\n56\t## Your answer\n57\t\n58\tWrite this JSON to C04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"C04\"):\n59\t```json\n60\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n61\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"C04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n62\t \"note\": \"one sent